WEBVTT

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:17.130
Nusumareta kako wo

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:20.330
Sagashitsuzukete

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:23.420
Ore wa samayou

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:27.130
Mishiranu machi wo

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:32.080
Honou no nioi shimitsuite

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:33.880
Museru

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:37.630
Sayonara wa itta hazu da

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:40.540
Wakareta hazu sa

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.790
Jigoku wo mireba

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.330
Kokoro ga kawaku

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:52.750
Tatakai wa akita no sa

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.540
Sadame to areba

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:00.790
Kokoro wo kimeru

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:05.960
Sottoshite oite kure

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:07.750
Ashita ni

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:15.250
Aa tsunagaru kyou gurai

00:01:31.790 --> 00:01:33.790
Just sleep for a little while.

00:01:33.790 --> 00:01:35.080
Although, when you wake up...

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:38.080
you may find yourself to be a different man.

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:11.500
Wait!

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:15.250
What are you? Monsters?

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:18.290
Stop! Stop it! We aren't monsters!

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:21.960
What the hell happened?

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:24.710
This is impossible!

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:31.040
Where are we?

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:33.130
And how did we get here?

00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:43.630
The Forbidden

00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:57.960
So, you're saying you instantly jumped
800 kilometers from where you were?

00:02:58.210 --> 00:03:01.790
No doubt about it, sir. We're back in Gomor.

00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:05.170
And whatever happened
almost seems like a dream now.

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:07.250
I want you to return to the ship at once!

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:08.750
You can give me the details here.

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:10.000
Understood, sir.

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:13.960
800 kilometers?

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:17.420
Just how advanced is the super-science
that's sleeping beneath this world?

00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:29.880
They vanished...

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:32.130
I'm sure I saw them vanish.

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:37.250
What's happening on this planet?

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:40.670
What's going on?

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:52.130
Neither the Gilgamesh nor the Balarant
have the information we now have on Quent.

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:57.580
Quent definitely appears to be a treasure trove
of technology of the highest level.

00:03:57.580 --> 00:04:01.580
And the inhabitants don't seem to have
any clue about the incredible artifacts

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:03.000
their own planet contains.

00:04:03.290 --> 00:04:09.000
The upper part of Gomor we teleported to
is apparently a forbidden zone for any Quentians.

00:04:09.830 --> 00:04:12.210
You're saying something's hidden here?

00:04:12.670 --> 00:04:15.460
Yes, Your Excellency. I think there's no doubt left.

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:16.710
Right, Arron?

00:04:17.170 --> 00:04:20.750
Yes. Don't you think we're
wasting our time on Chirico, sir?

00:04:23.170 --> 00:04:26.670
If we get the super-technology hidden here...

00:04:26.670 --> 00:04:30.170
control of the Astragius Galaxy
wouldn't just be a dream anymore.

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:32.710
And just what is that supposed to mean?

00:04:33.670 --> 00:04:35.330
Nothing, sir.

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:38.630
But we were moved 800 km in an instant.

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:43.330
And that looks like just a
small piece of Quent's science.

00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:53.380
Ha'de Gomor'ra mei…

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:56.210
Gomor? It was to Gomor?

00:04:56.210 --> 00:04:58.580
They were transported to Gomor?

00:04:58.580 --> 00:04:59.960
That's what he says.

00:04:59.960 --> 00:05:01.380
And he isn't wrong?

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:03.750
Meji is never wrong.

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:07.040
Ask him why they disappeared.

00:05:07.710 --> 00:05:09.960
Burah heboraa'de mih-haa?

00:05:09.960 --> 00:05:13.210
Sa'gura hibo'me rohla...

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:16.500
He says the power which protects Quent did it.

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:20.710
Hohra heboraa de'ho has'sha rah-daa...

00:05:20.710 --> 00:05:24.710
He says the power has done this
since long, long ago.

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:27.750
Does he understand how it was
able to transport them?

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:30.460
Zuhoh'va ohma do gua'vaa?

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:31.750
Noh-maa...

00:05:31.750 --> 00:05:33.880
He says he doesn't.

00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:36.000
What's that thing that looks like a factory?

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:38.420
Mi owa eraa'da miah?

00:05:38.420 --> 00:05:40.750
Noh-maa. E ria'miia zumaa...

00:05:40.750 --> 00:05:42.290
I don't think he knows.

00:05:42.290 --> 00:05:45.750
He says entry into there has been
forbidden since long ago.

00:05:46.420 --> 00:05:49.420
Are there any other forbidden areas?

00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:51.920
The nearest one is in Gomor.

00:05:51.920 --> 00:05:53.210
Gomor?

00:05:53.210 --> 00:05:54.500
That city?

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:59.000
The upper half's been forbidden to us
since ancient times.

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:06.960
You're saying your interest in this
is strictly as scientists?

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:08.540
Of course, sir.

00:06:10.420 --> 00:06:14.250
200 years ago, Commodore Hauzel,
intent on conquest,

00:06:14.250 --> 00:06:17.920
brought the 8th Balarant fleet
near the surface of Quent,

00:06:17.920 --> 00:06:20.670
which resulted in every ship
vanishing in an instant.

00:06:21.130 --> 00:06:23.380
The same thing happened 250 years ago.

00:06:23.380 --> 00:06:26.000
And 300 years ago, and before that.

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:27.420
And it happened today as well!

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:30.790
You were transported 800 kilometers instantly!

00:06:33.880 --> 00:06:38.080
Why don't the Balarant or the Gilgamesh
touch this treasure trove?

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:39.750
Because it's dangerous!

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:42.460
And now you want me to interfere with it?

00:06:42.830 --> 00:06:47.130
Sir, those aren't magicians or
sorcerers down there.

00:06:47.130 --> 00:06:48.790
And there is a way to do this.

00:06:48.790 --> 00:06:50.790
If we controlled Quent's science,

00:06:50.790 --> 00:06:54.080
then your dreams of controlling
the Astragius Galaxy might come true.

00:06:55.630 --> 00:07:01.500
As scientists, it's our duty to ascertain
whether or not that power exists on Quent.

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:15.750
Shall we wager?

00:07:15.750 --> 00:07:16.830
On what?

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:18.920
His approval of our conquest plan.

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:20.830
Please, don't even start.

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:24.630
Killy and the others are terrified of the old data.

00:07:25.500 --> 00:07:29.830
But I see ambition beginning to swirl in his heart.

00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:33.790
Is that your analysis of His Excellency?

00:07:33.790 --> 00:07:34.710
Exactly.

00:07:34.710 --> 00:07:37.380
So, you're seeing which way the scale is tipping.

00:07:37.380 --> 00:07:38.420
Bravo!

00:07:38.710 --> 00:07:41.170
I believe this is a critical time for him.

00:07:41.500 --> 00:07:45.250
You're an evil man, Big Brother.
Tempting His Excellency like that.

00:07:45.250 --> 00:07:47.170
You make me sound like a scoundrel!

00:07:47.170 --> 00:07:51.290
I was just letting him see
what the situation before him was.

00:07:51.540 --> 00:07:55.000
Consider this: Which is the more
respectable position?

00:07:55.000 --> 00:08:00.170
Commander of a society or
ruler of the Astragius Galaxy?

00:08:00.670 --> 00:08:02.040
What do you think, Big Brother?

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:05.500
Me? My interests lie purely in the field of science.

00:08:09.540 --> 00:08:11.920
The Astragius Galaxy...

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:19.580
Sir, we have a report.

00:08:19.580 --> 00:08:22.250
A fleet is approaching at 12 o'clock.

00:08:22.250 --> 00:08:25.290
At their current speed,
they will contact us in three hours.

00:08:25.290 --> 00:08:27.040
Ships' affiliation is not clear at this time.

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:28.710
Continue surveillance.

00:08:28.710 --> 00:08:29.630
Aye, sir.

00:08:31.210 --> 00:08:34.210
The Balarant? Or the Gilgamesh?

00:09:02.460 --> 00:09:05.960
The decision has to be now.
We only have three hours!

00:09:06.670 --> 00:09:08.080
Summon Arron and Gurran!

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:34.630
Control, we request landing clearance.

00:09:34.630 --> 00:09:38.130
We also wish to offload 100 crates
for the Mercenary Center.

00:09:38.130 --> 00:09:40.460
This is a shuttle from the
commercial transport Scintenna.

00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:43.880
This is control. You are cleared for landing.

00:11:17.750 --> 00:11:19.130
Results: Positive.

00:11:19.130 --> 00:11:21.670
Looks like we tricked them.

00:11:21.670 --> 00:11:24.670
They haven't guessed
what our true intentions are.

00:11:28.420 --> 00:11:29.880
Looks okay.

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:33.460
We're moving out.

00:11:33.460 --> 00:11:37.170
Remember, make no threatening
movements of any kind.

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:41.250
Any fighting will be on our command alone.

00:11:41.250 --> 00:11:42.830
At all costs, be careful.

00:11:43.710 --> 00:11:44.790
Prepare to move out.

00:12:20.290 --> 00:12:22.790
Stop! We mean you no harm!

00:12:27.380 --> 00:12:29.000
Isn't this risky, Big Brother?

00:12:29.000 --> 00:12:33.250
I know, but we've no choice.

00:12:33.250 --> 00:12:36.880
Uh, attention people of Gomor.
There's no cause for alarm.

00:12:36.880 --> 00:12:39.920
We're not here to hurt anyone.

00:12:39.920 --> 00:12:44.920
We'd just like to take control of
your city for a little while.

00:12:48.540 --> 00:12:51.630
Hmm... A town full of cowards?

00:12:51.630 --> 00:12:55.630
It would appear that way.
But it helps us in this case.

00:12:59.670 --> 00:13:03.130
Whose side are you on?
This is a nonaggression zone!

00:13:03.130 --> 00:13:06.170
Direct military action is forbidden on Quent!

00:13:09.710 --> 00:13:11.540
Wait! Don't shoot!

00:13:12.290 --> 00:13:15.830
We're not engaging in any direct military action!

00:13:15.830 --> 00:13:18.960
We're scientists, investigating this giant ruin!

00:13:19.210 --> 00:13:20.710
Do you think we're stupid?

00:13:20.710 --> 00:13:23.460
Are you saying you need
an AT force to investigate it?

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:42.330
We brought them because
they obviously are necessary.

00:13:42.330 --> 00:13:44.000
We're scientists!

00:13:44.000 --> 00:13:47.330
Are you planning on some
"direct military action"?

00:13:47.330 --> 00:13:49.080
You're the aggressors here.

00:13:50.630 --> 00:13:53.000
Go to Alert 3 status! Return to your posts!

00:13:53.000 --> 00:13:54.000
Return to posts!

00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:56.250
Is this clear? Take no action in the city!

00:13:59.960 --> 00:14:01.330
Take no action!

00:14:01.330 --> 00:14:04.630
Until we get orders from Melkia HQ,
keep our troops out of this!

00:14:04.630 --> 00:14:06.170
Let the police handle this!

00:14:06.170 --> 00:14:07.040
Yes, sir!

00:14:09.000 --> 00:14:11.330
We've no intention of attacking.

00:14:11.330 --> 00:14:13.670
Shall we proceed with the investigation, Arron?

00:14:13.670 --> 00:14:15.170
Let's go, let's go.

00:14:15.670 --> 00:14:17.790
Two units will remain here for the police.

00:14:17.790 --> 00:14:19.460
The rest, move out!

00:14:26.380 --> 00:14:29.460
Okay? Nobody shoot first, no matter what!

00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:03.420
What's wrong?

00:15:03.420 --> 00:15:04.460
What's that?

00:15:05.080 --> 00:15:06.250
The beacon.

00:15:06.250 --> 00:15:07.250
The beacon?

00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:09.080
Something's happened in Gomor.

00:15:09.710 --> 00:15:13.040
That stone's telling me.
Something bad has happened.

00:15:13.040 --> 00:15:14.040
Come on!

00:15:14.420 --> 00:15:17.080
We won't make it. Gomor's far from here.

00:15:19.670 --> 00:15:21.330
Let's get back to the cave, then.

00:15:24.250 --> 00:15:25.380
Hurry!

00:15:43.460 --> 00:15:47.000
All right, send two units out
from the front to scout the area.

00:16:04.080 --> 00:16:05.210
Damn!

00:16:30.170 --> 00:16:32.580
It looks like the devices we saw
in the Quentian village.

00:16:36.130 --> 00:16:38.130
Do you think this city...?

00:16:38.670 --> 00:16:39.750
Probably.

00:16:40.170 --> 00:16:42.790
Looks safe enough. Any readings?

00:16:42.790 --> 00:16:43.750
Hold on.

00:16:50.830 --> 00:16:51.920
Well?

00:16:52.500 --> 00:16:53.920
Nothing unusual.

00:16:54.420 --> 00:16:57.170
Idiot, after all our warnings to be careful.

00:16:57.170 --> 00:16:59.670
Two units, stay here. The rest, move out.

00:17:25.750 --> 00:17:26.710
Is that it?

00:17:43.250 --> 00:17:48.080
Gentlemen, I remind you:
no threatening movements.

00:18:31.960 --> 00:18:33.880
What are you planning to do here?

00:18:33.880 --> 00:18:36.040
Get it to take us to Gomor, too.

00:18:37.130 --> 00:18:38.380
I'm going to try something.

00:18:38.380 --> 00:18:44.210
Unless I'm wrong, the power that protects Quent
reacts to the sound and movement of machines.

00:19:23.830 --> 00:19:24.670
Shako!

00:19:27.290 --> 00:19:28.750
I'm okay.

00:19:34.960 --> 00:19:36.330
This is Gomor, all right.

00:19:39.670 --> 00:19:40.960
Yeah...

00:19:46.630 --> 00:19:48.500
What are you doing over there?

00:19:50.960 --> 00:19:53.210
Shako, we're stealing that AT.

00:19:53.710 --> 00:19:54.880
Gotcha.

00:19:56.330 --> 00:19:58.250
I saw a strange man over here.

00:19:58.250 --> 00:19:59.750
A strange man?

00:20:00.210 --> 00:20:01.170
Where?

00:20:01.170 --> 00:20:02.420
Right behind you.

00:20:02.420 --> 00:20:03.250
What?

00:20:04.250 --> 00:20:05.630
Who the hell?

00:20:19.330 --> 00:20:20.170
Let's go!

00:20:27.540 --> 00:20:29.460
Mr. Arron! We have traitors in the ranks!

00:20:46.750 --> 00:20:48.250
You don't suppose...

00:20:48.750 --> 00:20:50.830
Something's approaching us.

00:20:50.830 --> 00:20:52.420
I read two metal objects.

00:20:52.420 --> 00:20:53.500
Chirico?

00:20:53.500 --> 00:20:54.460
Maybe.

00:20:58.420 --> 00:21:00.460
That's him, all right!

00:21:01.040 --> 00:21:03.580
Isn't it a bad idea to start shooting in here?

00:21:03.580 --> 00:21:07.250
What choice do we have? Hope for the best.

00:21:07.250 --> 00:21:08.210
Destroy the intruders!

00:21:49.040 --> 00:21:52.040
Even this level of fighting doesn't trigger it.

00:21:52.040 --> 00:21:54.040
Yeah... Looks like we're safe.

00:22:08.460 --> 00:22:09.420
Again?

00:22:25.000 --> 00:22:26.380
Shako, kill your engine!

00:22:26.380 --> 00:22:28.420
Shut down every system on the AT!

00:22:42.540 --> 00:22:45.580
Again! It was happening just as I'd predicted.

00:22:46.420 --> 00:22:48.420
Where would it transport us to this time?

00:22:48.880 --> 00:22:52.130
And what had we set into motion?

00:22:53.540 --> 00:22:54.960
Next Episode

00:22:55.130 --> 00:22:56.540
To Quent.

00:22:56.880 --> 00:23:04.210
To the frontier world which hides the greatest
of mysteries. All power. All ambitions.

00:23:05.170 --> 00:23:09.330
Is what dwells in its depths God or Satan?

00:23:10.210 --> 00:23:15.920
The mystery winds back into history,
and a flash of light reveals deep desires.

00:23:16.630 --> 00:23:18.880
Next time, "Contact"

00:23:19.040 --> 00:23:23.500
Contact

00:23:19.040 --> 00:23:23.500
Next Time

00:23:19.500 --> 00:23:21.960
A shudder tempts them towards the center.

00:23:41.750 --> 00:23:45.210
Samishii toki mo

00:23:45.210 --> 00:23:48.750
Kanashii toki mo

00:23:48.750 --> 00:23:55.170
Itsumo anata ga me ni ukabu

00:23:55.630 --> 00:23:59.170
Hitori no toki mo

00:23:59.170 --> 00:24:02.630
Aitai toki mo

00:24:02.630 --> 00:24:08.830
Itsumo anata wa mune no naka

00:24:08.830 --> 00:24:12.330
Tooku hanarete itemo

00:24:12.330 --> 00:24:15.750
Tatoe wakarete itemo

00:24:15.960 --> 00:24:22.250
Kono yo no hikari to tomo ni mabushiku

00:24:22.670 --> 00:24:28.580
Ano hi no anata ga...
